# PCB Defect Detection — Core Rules

Stack: PyTorch, FastAPI, MLflow, Kafka (apache/kafka, KRaft), Docker, pytest.
Never suggest TensorFlow, Keras, YOLO, Kubernetes, Redis, Postgres, Airflow,
DVC, ONNX, or Prometheus. All are deliberately out of scope.

## Task shape
- Patch-level classification, NOT whole-image. 64x64 grayscale patches tiled
  from 640x640 DeepPCB boards.
- 7 classes: good, open, short, mousebite, spur, copper, pinhole.
- Model input is (B, 1, 64, 64). Single channel. No colour augmentation.
- Train/val/test splits are by source image, never by patch. Splitting after
  tiling leaks correlated patches across splits.

## Model
- PCBNet: 4 conv blocks (32/64/128/256), Conv-BN-ReLU x2 then MaxPool.
- Global Average Pooling head into one Linear layer. Never Flatten into a
  large dense layer - GAP is required for Grad-CAM.

## Metrics
- Select models on macro F1. Never on accuracy.
- Headline metric is binary defect recall (six defect classes collapsed).
- Loss is class-weighted by inverse frequency.

## Gitignore
Patterns must be root-anchored (/data/, not data/). A bare data/ also
matches src/data/ and would silently untrack build_patches.py.

## Environment
- Days 1-4 run on Colab (T4). Days 5-9 run locally on an 8GB M-series Mac.
- Notebooks are thin drivers: they call scripts in src/. No model definitions
  or training loops in notebook cells.
